2026-05-17 14:13:30,226 DEBUG msg #32: UserMessage tool_result(functions.Read:0): 1	# stockpy 0.4.x — Forecaster Requirements
2	
3	This document is the authoritative specification for the forecasting models in
4	`stockpy`. It covers (a) the canonical encoder–decoder forecasters that already
5	ship in `stockpy/forecasters/`, and (b) two new encoder-only Transformer
6	forecasters — `PatchTSTForecaster` and `iTransformerForecaster` — to be added.
7	
8	The architectural rationale: recent literature (Liu et al. 2024, Nie et al.
9	2023, arXiv 2507.13043) shows that direct-mapping encoder-only Transformers
10	outperform autoregressive seq2seq on long-horizon multivariate benchmarks
11	because they avoid error accumulation. Classical seq2seq RNNs and the vanilla
12	encoder–decoder Transformer remain valuable as pedagogical baselines and on
13	short horizons. stockpy therefore offers both paradigms behind a single
14	`EncoderDecoderForecaster` API contract.
15	
16	---
17	
18	## 1. Library invariants
19	
20	All forecasters MUST satisfy the following:
21	
22	- Subclass `EncoderDecoderForecaster` (`stockpy/base.py:4594`).
23	- Constructor accepts `context_len: int`, `pred_len: int`, and forwards
24	  `**kwargs` to `super().__init__`.
25	- Every public ctor parameter is stored as-is on the instance under the same
26	  name (sklearn convention — required for `get_params()`).
27	- `module_.forward(x, y=None) -> Tensor` returns shape
28	  `(batch, pred_len, n_features)`.
29	- `predict(X)` returns `numpy.ndarray` of shape
30	  `(n_windows, pred_len, n_features)`.
31	- Model state persisted via **safetensors** only (`save_params` /
32	  `load_params`). Never `torch.save`.
33	- Probabilistic models set `self._is_probabilistic = True` and use Pyro SVI;
34	  the new models specified in §3–§4 are deterministic.
35	- File naming: `stockpy/forecasters/_<name>.py`, class `<Name>Forecaster`.
36	  Encoder/decoder/backbone sub-modules live as private classes inside the same
37	  file (exception: `_dmm_components.py`, kept separate because `Combiner` /
38	  `Emitter` / `Transition` are reused by Pyro `model` and `guide`).
39	- First import in every `_*.py` is `from __future__ import annotations`.
40	- NumPy-style docstrings on all public methods.
41	- Black 88-char line length; pycodestyle clean.
42	- Full type annotations on `__init__`, `forward`, and `initialize_module`.
43	  `initialize_module` returns `Self` (or the concrete subclass).
44	- `model_type` attribute returns `"rnn"` (drives the data-iterator selector in
45	  the base class; the name is historical and applies to all sequence
46	  forecasters regardless of internal architecture). See
47	  `stockpy/forecasters/_transformer.py:304-309` for the canonical comment.
48	
49	### 1.1 Required base-class hooks (every concrete forecaster)
50	
51	The following overrides are non-optional. They are present in every existing
52	forecaster and must be replicated identically in the new ones.
53	
54	- `self._modules = ["module"]` set in `__init__` so
55	  `_initialize_module` (`base.py:1271-1298`) can locate `module_` for
56	  device placement.
57	- Override `state_dict()` and `load_state_dict()` to delegate to
58	  `self.module_` (see `_lstm.py:240-248`, `_transformer.py:296-300`).
59	  Without this, safetensors save/load silently round-trips the wrong tensors.
60	- Override `_set_training(training)` to call `self.module_.train(training)`
61	  (see `_lstm.py:206-208`). Without this, dropout stays active during
62	  `predict()`.
63	- Define `__sklearn_tags__` and `_get_tags` identically to the existing
64	  `TransformerForecaster` (`_transformer.py:247-257`).
65	
66	### 1.2 Constructor invariants for new (non-teacher-forcing) forecasters
67	
68	Models in §3 and §4 are direct-multi-step. They do **not** override
69	`train_step_single`. The base `train_step_single` (`base.py:1769-1773`) does
70	not pass `y` to `forward`, so the "forward ignores `y`" contract is satisfied
71	without further wiring. Implementors MUST NOT add a teacher-forcing override
72	for these models.
73	
74	---
75	
76	## 2. Canonical encoder–decoder forecasters (existing)
77	
78	These ship today in `stockpy/forecasters/`. They are the reference
79	implementation of the **encoder–decoder seq2seq** paradigm. No code changes
80	required by this document — they are listed here so the spec is complete.
81	
82	| Forecaster              | File              | Encoder                                    | Decoder                                  | Decode strategy                                      |
83	| ----------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
84	| `LSTMForecaster`        | `_lstm.py`        | `nn.LSTM`                                  | `nn.LSTM` + linear output projection     | Teacher forcing during training, autoregressive at inference |
85	| `GRUForecaster`         | `_gru.py`         | `nn.GRU`                                   | `nn.GRU` + linear output projection      | Same as LSTM                                         |
86	| `BiLSTMForecaster`      | `_bilstm.py`      | bidirectional `nn.LSTM`                    | unidirectional `nn.LSTM`                 | Hidden state projected before decoder                |
87	| `BiGRUForecaster`       | `_bigru.py`       | bidirectional `nn.GRU`                     | unidirectional `nn.GRU`                  | Hidden state projected before decoder                |
88	| `TransformerForecaster` | `_transformer.py` | `nn.TransformerEncoder` + sinusoidal posenc | `nn.TransformerDecoder` (cross-attn)     | Causal `tgt_mask`; teacher-forced training, autoregressive inference |
89	| `TCNForecaster`         | `_tcn.py`         | dilated causal `Conv1d` stack              | `nn.GRU` decoder                         | Encoder produces context vector; GRU decodes         |
90	| `DMMForecaster`         | `_dmm.py`         | RNN encoder (`guide`)                      | Markov latent emission (`model`)         | Pyro SVI with `TraceMeanField_ELBO`                  |
91	
92	Constructor signatures, default hyperparameters, and decode logic are defined
93	in those files and are considered frozen for this release.
94	
95	---
96	
97	## 3. New forecaster: `PatchTSTForecaster`
98	
99	**Reference**: Nie, Nguyen, Sinthong, Kalagnanam,
100	*A Time Series is Worth 64 Words: Long-term Forecasting with Transformers*,
101	ICLR 2023.
102	
103	**Paradigm**: encoder-only Transformer with **channel-independent**
104	processing and a direct multi-step head. The encoder–decoder ABC is satisfied
105	by the `context_len → pred_len` mapping contract; there is no literal decoder
106	module.
107	
108	### 3.1 File and class
109	
110	- New file: `stockpy/forecasters/_patchtst.py`.
111	- Class: `PatchTSTForecaster(EncoderDecoderForecaster)`.
112	
113	### 3.2 Constructor
114	
115	```python
116	def __init__(
117	    self,
118	    patch_len: int = 16,
119	    stride: int = 8,
120	    d_model: int = 128,
121	    nhead: int = 16,
122	    num_layers: int = 3,
123	    dim_feedforward: int = 512,
124	    dropout: float = 0.2,
125	    activation: str = "gelu",
126	    revin: bool = True,
127	    revin_affine: bool = True,
128	    context_len: int = 96,
129	    pred_len: int = 24,
130	    **kwargs,
131	) -> None: ...
132	```
133	
134	All parameters stored as-is on `self`.
135	
136	**`__init__` validation (raise `ValueError` on bad combinations):**
137	
138	- `context_len < patch_len` → unfold impossible.
139	- `d_model % nhead != 0` → `nn.MultiheadAttention` requires divisibility.
140	- `patch_len < 1` or `stride < 1` → invalid window.
141	
142	**Default note:** `dim_feedforward = 4 * d_model` follows standard Transformer
143	ratios (paper uses GELU, ratio ≈ 4×). `nhead=16, d_model=128` gives head_dim=8
144	matching Nie et al. ICLR 2023.
145	
146	### 3.3 Architecture (forward pass)
147	
148	Input shape `(B, L, C)` where `L == context_len`, `C == n_features`.
149	
150	1. **RevIN** (reversible instance normalization), if `revin=True`. Compute
151	   per-(batch, feature) mean and standard deviation over the time axis;
152	   subtract and divide. Return `(x_norm, mean, std)` from the RevIN
153	   `_normalize` call; pass `mean` and `std` as **local tensors through the
154	   call stack** to the inverse step. Do NOT cache statistics as `nn.Module`
155	   attributes — that breaks under repeated/concurrent forward passes.
156	2. Permute to `(B, C, L)`.
157	3. **Patching with end-padding**: replicate-pad the right edge of the time
158	   axis so that `(L_padded - patch_len)` is divisible by `stride`, matching
159	   the original PatchTST reference implementation. Then unfold with window
160	   `patch_len` and `stride`. Result shape `(B, C, N, patch_len)` where
161	   `N = floor((L_padded - patch_len) / stride) + 1`. With default
162	   `context_len=96, patch_len=16, stride=8`, `L_padded=104` and `N=12`.
163	4. **Channel independence**: reshape to `(B * C, N, patch_len)`. The
164	   Transformer backbone weights are shared across all `C` features.
165	5. **Patch embedding**: `nn.Linear(patch_len, d_model)` + learnable positional
166	   embedding of shape `(N, d_model)`.
167	6. **Transformer encoder**: `nn.TransformerEncoder` with `num_layers` layers,
168	   post-norm, `batch_first=True`. Activation `gelu` by default.
169	7. **Flatten head**: flatten `(B * C, N * d_model)` → `nn.Linear(N * d_model,
170	   pred_len)` → `(B * C, pred_len)`.
171	8. Reshape to `(B, C, pred_len)`. Permute to `(B, pred_len, C)`. If RevIN
172	   active, multiply by `std` and add `mean` (the local tensors threaded
173	   through from step 1).
174	
175	### 3.4 Private modules in `_patchtst.py`
176	
177	All sub-modules are private (leading underscore) per §1. Only
178	`PatchTSTForecaster` appears in this module's `__all__`.
179	
180	```python
181	class _RevIN(nn.Module):
182	    """Reversible instance norm. Affine gamma/beta lazily allocated on
183	    first forward call once n_features is known. eps=1e-5."""
184	    def __init__(self, num_features: int, affine: bool = True,
185	                 eps: float = 1e-5) -> None: ...
186	    def _normalize(self, x: Tensor) -> tuple[Tensor, Tensor, Tensor]: ...
187	    def _denormalize(self, x: Tensor, mean: Tensor, std: Tensor) -> Tensor: ...
188	
189	class _PatchEmbedding(nn.Module):
190	    """Unfold + linear + learnable positional embedding."""
191	    def __init__(self, patch_len: int, stride: int, d_model: int,
192	                 num_patches: int) -> None: ...
193	
194	class _PatchTSTModel(nn.Module):
195	    """Top-level module used by the forecaster. Composes RevIN +
196	    patch embedding + nn.TransformerEncoder + flatten head."""
197	    def __init__(self, n_features: int, context_len: int, pred_len: int,
198	                 patch_len: int, stride: int, d_model: int, nhead: int,
199	                 num_layers: int, dim_feedforward: int, dropout: float,
200	                 activation: str, revin: bool,
201	                 revin_affine: bool) -> None: ...
202	    def forward(self, x: Tensor, y: Tensor | None = None) -> Tensor: ...
203	```
204	
205	`gamma` and `beta` of `_RevIN` are learnable `nn.Parameter` tensors of shape
206	`(num_features,)` when `affine=True`; allocated in `_PatchTSTModel.__init__`
207	because `n_features` is known there (passed from `initialize_module` via
208	`self.n_features_in_`).
209	
210	### 3.5 Training and loss
211	
212	- `initialize_module` builds `_PatchTSTModel` with stored hyperparameters
213	  plus `self.n_features_in_` and `self.context_len`, then sets
214	  `self.criterion_ = nn.MSELoss()`.
215	- `forward` ignores `y` — direct multi-step head, no teacher forcing,
216	  no `train_step_single` override (see §1.2).
217	- **Recommended optimizer: Adam.** SGD (the base default) will not converge
218	  for this architecture. Spec consumers SHOULD pass
219	  `optimizer=torch.optim.Adam` and `lr=1e-3` at fit time, or override
220	  defaults at the forecaster ctor. The `test_fit_on_synthetic_data` test
221	  MUST pass `optimizer=Adam`.
222	
223	---
224	
225	## 4. New forecaster: `iTransformerForecaster`
226	
227	**Reference**: Liu, Hu, Liu, Zhang, Wang, Long,
228	*iTransformer: Inverted Transformers Are Effective for Time Series
229	Forecasting*, ICLR 2024.
230	
231	**Paradigm**: encoder-only Transformer where each **variate** (feature) is one
232	token. Self-attention is computed across variates, capturing
233	multivariate cross-feature dependence. There is no positional encoding because
234	variates are an unordered set.
235	
236	### 4.1 File and class
237	
238	- New file: `stockpy/forecasters/_itransformer.py`.
239	- Class: `iTransformerForecaster(EncoderDecoderForecaster)`.
240	
241	### 4.2 Constructor
242	
243	```python
244	def __init__(
245	    self,
246	    d_model: int = 128,
247	    nhead: int = 8,
248	    num_layers: int = 3,
249	    dim_feedforward: int = 512,
250	    dropout: float = 0.1,
251	    activation: str = "gelu",
252	    use_norm: bool = True,
253	    context_len: int = 96,
254	    pred_len: int = 24,
255	    **kwargs,
256	) -> None: ...
257	```
258	
259	**`__init__` validation (raise `ValueError` on bad combinations):**
260	
261	- `d_model % nhead != 0` → `nn.MultiheadAttention` requires divisibility.
262	- `context_len < 1` or `pred_len < 1` → invalid window.
263	
264	### 4.3 Architecture (forward pass)
265	
266	Input shape `(B, L, C)`.
267	
268	1. **Series-wise normalization**, if `use_norm=True`. Compute per-(batch,
269	   feature) mean and standard deviation over the time axis; subtract and
270	   divide. Pass `mean` and `std` as **local tensors through the call stack**
271	   to step 6. Do NOT store on `nn.Module`.
272	2. Permute to `(B, C, L)`.
273	3. **Variate embedding**: `nn.Linear(L, d_model)` applied per variate →
274	   `(B, C, d_model)`. Each of the `C` rows is now one token.
275	4. **Transformer encoder**: `nn.TransformerEncoder` with `num_layers` layers,
276	   `batch_first=True`. **No positional encoding** — variates are unordered.
277	   Self-attention thus attends across variates rather than across time.
278	5. **Projection head**: `nn.Linear(d_model, pred_len)` per token →
279	   `(B, C, pred_len)`.
280	6. Permute to `(B, pred_len, C)`. If normalization active, restore using
281	   `mean` and `std` (local tensors threaded through from step 1).
282	
283	### 4.4 Private modules in `_itransformer.py`
284	
285	All sub-modules are private (leading underscore) per §1. Only
286	`iTransformerForecaster` appears in this module's `__all__`.
287	
288	```python
289	class _iTransformerEmbedding(nn.Module):
290	    """Per-variate linear projection L -> d_model. Shared weights across
291	    all C variates."""
292	    def __init__(self, context_len: int, d_model: int) -> None: ...
293	
294	class _iTransformerModel(nn.Module):
295	    """Top-level module. Composes per-variate embedding +
296	    nn.TransformerEncoder (no posenc) + per-variate projection head."""
297	    def __init__(self, context_len: int, pred_len: int, d_model: int,
298	                 nhead: int, num_layers: int, dim_feedforward: int,
299	                 dropout: float, activation: str, use_norm: bool) -> None: ...
300	    def forward(self, x: Tensor, y: Tensor | None = None) -> Tensor: ...
301	```
302	
303	The projection head is a single shared `nn.Linear(d_model, pred_len)` applied
304	per token; weights are not per-variate. `n_features_in_` is therefore not
305	needed at module construction time.
306	
307	### 4.5 Training and loss
308	
309	- `initialize_module` builds `_iTransformerModel` with stored hyperparameters
310	  plus `self.context_len`, then sets `self.criterion_ = nn.MSELoss()`.
311	- `forward` ignores `y`. No `train_step_single` override (see §1.2).
312	- **Recommended optimizer: Adam.** Same rationale as PatchTST.
313	  `test_fit_on_synthetic_data` MUST pass `optimizer=Adam`.
314	
315	---
316	
317	## 5. Public API registration
318	
319	Update `stockpy/forecasters/__init__.py`:
320	
321	- Add imports:
322	  ```python
323	  from ._patchtst import *
324	  from ._itransformer import *
325	  ```
326	- Append to `__all__`:
327	  ```python
328	  "PatchTSTForecaster",
329	  "iTransformerForecaster",
330	  ```
331	
332	Each new `_*.py` file declares its own `__all__` listing only the
333	`<Name>Forecaster` symbol.
334	
335	No changes to `pyproject.toml` (no new runtime dependencies — both models use
336	`torch.nn.TransformerEncoder` and standard ops already pulled in).
337	
338	---
339	
340	## 6. Tests
341	
342	For each new forecaster, create
343	`test/test_<name>_forecaster.py` mirroring
344	`test/test_transformer_forecaster.py`. Required cases:
345	
346	1. `test_is_subclass_of_encoder_decoder_forecaster` — `issubclass` check.
347	2. `test_instantiation_sets_context_and_pred_len` — ctor wiring.
348	3. `test_model_type_attribute` — equals `"rnn"`.
349	4. `test_initialize_module_creates_module_` — `module_` and `criterion_` set.
350	5. Architecture-specific:
351	   - **PatchTST**:
352	     - `test_patch_count_correct` — with end-padding,
353	       N = floor((L_padded − patch_len)/stride) + 1; assert against the
354	       backbone's stored `num_patches` attribute.
355	     - `test_revin_round_trip` — fit a model on a constant series and verify
356	       output equals input within `atol=1e-5`.
357	     - `test_channel_independence_shared_weights` — build two models with
358	       `n_features=1` and `n_features=8`, assert
359	       `sum(p.numel() for p in model.module_.parameters())` differs only by
360	       the RevIN affine params (`2 * n_features` when `revin_affine=True`).
361	     - `test_invalid_ctor_raises` — `context_len < patch_len`,
362	       `d_model % nhead != 0`, `patch_len < 1`, `stride < 1` each raise
363	       `ValueError`.
364	   - **iTransformer**:
365	     - `test_variate_token_axis` — register a forward hook on the inner
366	       `TransformerEncoder` and assert its input has shape `(B, C, d_model)`,
367	       not `(B, L, d_model)`.
368	     - `test_invalid_ctor_raises` — `d_model % nhead != 0` raises `ValueError`.
369	6. `test_forward_output_shape` — output is `(B, pred_len, n_features)`.
370	7. `test_predict_returns_correct_shape` — predict on synthetic series.
371	8. `test_fit_on_synthetic_data` — uses `stockpy.preprocessing._synthetic`,
372	   passes `optimizer=torch.optim.Adam`, `lr=1e-3`; loss decreases monotonically
373	   over the first 5 epochs (use a small fixed seed).
374	9. `test_save_load_roundtrip(tmp_path)` — instantiate with `dropout=0.0`,
375	   call `model.module_.eval()` before both prediction calls, then assert
376	   predictions match within `atol=1e-6`. (Stochastic dropout would otherwise
377	   make the round-trip flaky.)
378	
379	The annotation contract test (`test/test_forecaster_annotations.py`) discovers
380	new files in `stockpy/forecasters/` automatically; both new files MUST
381	therefore start with `from __future__ import annotations` and provide complete
382	type hints on `__init__`, `forward`, and `initialize_module`.
383	
